   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Text Reveal\n\nWords appear one at a time: a flowing, halftone-textured light material fills the letters, then clears to clean white type before a dark wave removes the word. Drawn in WebGL over a transparent background.\n\nCategory: shaders. Length: 2.5 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A short headline needs a shader reveal, one word at a time.\n- The material should appear inside letters before they settle into white.\n\nAvoid when:\n- A quiet text entrance is enough: use soft-blur-in.\n- Words should physically morph into each other: use kinetic-morph-text.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Your product\"\n- font_size (number, 24-500): Font size, default 400\n- font_family (string): Font, default \"Arial, sans-serif\"\n- font_weight (number, 100-900): Weight, default 500\n- word_duration (number, 12-90): Frames per word, default 30\n- intensity (number, 0-1): Shader strength, default 1\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.5\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
